-- matdo (2026-10-04, agent quaimatdo): "Mat do & hoi quai" - more field monsters and a shorter revive time,
-- set from AdminWeb (tab "Mat do & hoi quai"). Generated by scratchpad\matdo\gen_matdo.py; ASCII only.
-- servertimer.lua PTAdm_ExtTick() loads this file and calls PTEXT_matdo_Tick() once per minute (protected).
--
-- Config admin_bridge\matdo_config.lua (AdminWeb writes it, read every tick; kept across server restarts):
--   PTMD_CFG = { density = 20, revive = 10, all = 1, maps = { 1006, 1026 } }
--   density = factor x10 (10 = x1, 15 = x1.5, 20 = x2, 30 = x3); revive = seconds after death (0 = Npcs.txt
--   ReviveFrame); all = 1: every map of PTMD_MAPS, all = 0: only the listed maps (the others go back to x1 and
--   to the Npcs.txt revive time).
-- Density: extra monsters of the same template and level 2-4 cells around the existing spawn points: the
--   spawn_main.lua rows PT_SPAWN_DATA (generated maps) and the VNG Region_S monsters of 1014/1016 (found by one
--   scan). AddNpc as in spawn_main.lua gives the template DeathScript (npc_quests\normal.lua: EXP, item drops,
--   kill quests, pet EXP), AI, camp and ReviveFrame; PTMD_Bind adds the ActionScript the originals of that
--   template get (spawn_main mob_drop.lua, newbie2 nb2_mob.lua, sudo_dongdi / questfix3 drop scripts).
--   Tracking by table, never by name: (map, slot e) -> npc index + GetNpcID; slot e always maps to the same seed,
--   so ticks and reloads never duplicate. Extras carry npc param 12 = PTMD_TAG (11 = slot, 13 = map): a fresh
--   script state adopts them (duplicates deleted). Lowering the factor deletes the highest slots first.
--   NPC budget: GetNpcCount() stays <= PTMD_CAP (engine MAX_NPC 48000). Maps with a player (and 15 minutes after
--   he left) get the full factor first; the other maps share the remaining budget proportionally.
-- Revive: SetNpcRevTime(npc, seconds * 18) on the field population (spawn_main PT_SPAWN_NPCS without the quest
--   specials, the region monsters, the extras). Bosses, quest monsters and feature NPCs are never touched.
--   Applied at once to the living monsters (a monster already waiting to revive keeps its current timer).
-- Lua 4: no true/false, no local function; data written one statement per record (120-slot engine stack).
